## Mandatory Coverage Check — MUST Print Before Completing Any Test Task

Every time you create or modify tests for a feature, you MUST output this matrix:

```
### Test Coverage Matrix — [Feature Name]
| # | Test Type | Status | File(s) | Test Count | Min Required | Pass? |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| T1 | Positive | ✅ Exists / ❌ Missing | [file path] | X | 3+ | ✅/❌ |
| T2 | Negative | ✅/❌ | [file path] | X | 3×P | ✅/❌ |
| T3 | Boundary | ✅/❌ | [file path] | X | 3×P | ✅/❌ |
| T4 | Functional | ✅/❌ | [file path] | X | 3×P | ✅/❌ |
| T5 | Integration | ✅/❌ | [file path] | X | 3×P | ✅/❌ |
| T6 | Unit | ✅/❌ | [file path] | X | 5+ | ✅/❌ |
| T7 | Concurrency | ✅/❌ | [file path] | X | 3+ | ✅/❌ |
| T8 | Performance | ✅/❌ | [file path] | X | 3+ | ✅/❌ |
| T9 | Load | ✅/❌ | [file path] | X | 3+ | ✅/❌ |
| T10 | Data Entry Perm. | ✅/❌ | [file path] | X | 10+ | ✅/❌ |
| T11 | Security | ✅/❌ | [file path] | X | (cross-cutting) | ✅/❌ |
| T12 | API Contract | ✅/❌ | [file path] | X | 5+ | ✅/❌ |
| T13 | Accessibility | ✅/❌ | [file path] | X | (cross-cutting) | ✅/❌ |
| T14 | i18n | ✅/❌ | [file path] | X | (cross-cutting) | ✅/❌ |
| T15 | Error Recovery | ✅/❌ | [file path] | X | 5+ | ✅/❌ |
| T16 | Rate Limiting | ✅/❌ | [file path] | X | (cross-cutting) | ✅/❌ |
```

If **any** Tier 1 or Tier 2 check is ❌, you MUST create the missing tests before proceeding.
If **any** Tier 3 check is ❌, you MUST flag it in your response and add it to the Coverage Dashboard.

---

## When This Rule Applies

### During Test Creation (create-tests agent or manual)
1. **Before generating tests**: Check what test types already exist for the feature
2. **After generating tests**: Print the full coverage matrix
3. **If gaps exist**: Create missing test types or document why they're deferred

### During Code Review
1. **Verify Tier 1 coverage**: All 5 core types must exist
2. **Check Tier 2 coverage**: All 5 extended types should exist
3. **Flag Tier 3 gaps**: Note any missing cross-cutting types

### During Sprint Planning
1. **Review Coverage Dashboard**: `QA Tests/COVERAGE_DASHBOARD.md`
2. **Prioritize gap closure**: Address ❌ items by priority tier
3. **Track progress**: Update dashboard after each sprint

---

## How to Add a New Test Type

If a new test category is identified (e.g., "Chaos Engineering", "Contract Testing"):

1. Add it to the appropriate tier in this rule
2. Define the Trait value, minimum count, and file pattern
3. Update the Coverage Dashboard template
4. Update the `create-tests` agent to include it
5. Create a tracking issue for retroactive coverage

