## Common Mistakes to Avoid

- ❌ Creating only Tier 1 tests and skipping Tier 2/3 entirely
- ❌ Assuming "integration tests" covers API contract testing (they're different)
- ❌ Treating accessibility as "Playwright only" — backend accessibility validation exists too
- ❌ Skipping data entry permutation tests because "negative tests cover it" — they don't test field ordering and combinations
- ❌ Deferring cross-cutting tests to "later sprints" without tracking them
- ❌ Not checking the Coverage Dashboard before starting a new test suite
- ❌ Creating test files without the proper `[Trait("Category", "...")]` attribute
- ❌ Forgetting to update the Coverage Dashboard after creating new tests
